<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Exclusion limits at 95% confidence level (CL) on the sum of the production cross-section times branching ratio of quantum black holes in the ADD model with <math id="S6.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=6</annotation></semantics></math> extra dimensions for the (a) electron and (b) muon channels, and in the RS model with <math id="S6.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math> extra dimension for the (c) electron and (d) muon channels. The <math id="S6.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 1\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 1\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 2\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 2\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> uncertainty bands around the expected limit are shown. The central theoretical values are overlaid. The summation subscript <math id="S6.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="qq^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">qq^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the three relevant production channels of the quantum black hole. The branching fraction used is per lepton flavour.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The RS model is excluded at 95% CL for signals with <math id="S6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\textrm{th}}&lt;7.2\penalty\ \textrm{TeV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>7.2</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>TeV</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\textrm{th}}&lt;7.2\penalty\ \textrm{TeV}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Depending on the number of EDs, ADD models with <math id="S6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\textrm{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\textrm{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> below 8.6–9.4 TeV are excluded at 95% CL.
The observed and expected <math id="S6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\textrm{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\textrm{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> exclusion limits at 95% CL for the signal models considered are detailed in Table <a href="#S6.T2" title='Table 2 ‣ 6 Results ‣ Search for quantum black holes in lepton+jet final states using proton–proton collisions at √𝑠=13.6⁢"TeV" with the ATLAS detector' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
The electron channel surpasses the muon channel in sensitivity by a factor of <math id="S6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sim}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sim}3</annotation></semantics></math>, due to better momentum resolution for electrons and its impact on the acceptance times efficiency, as well as the lower background in the SR.
Hence, the two channels are not combined.</p>
</div>
