<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This ATLAS analysis is performed using <math id="S7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="164\penalty\ \textrm{fb}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>164</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>fb</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">164\penalty\ \textrm{fb}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> of data collected from <math id="S7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{s}=13.6\penalty\ \textrm{TeV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>s</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>13.6</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>TeV</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{s}=13.6\penalty\ \textrm{TeV}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pp</annotation></semantics></math> collisions at the LHC.
The search for QBH-like signals yields no evidence of an excess in the lepton+jet invariant mass distribution in electron+jet or muon+jet final states.
Exclusion limits are placed on the production cross-section times branching ratio in a few ADD and RS QBH scenarios. The experimental sensitivity is driven by the statistical uncertainty.
The highest exclusion limits are for ADD QBH scenarios with six extra dimensions, observed at 9.4 TeV (9.0 TeV) in the electron (muon) channel.
Owing to the much better momentum resolution and larger acceptance times efficiency in the electron channel, the sensitivity is significantly higher.
This analysis extends the mass-exclusion reach of the previous ATLAS search performed at <math id="S7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{s}=13\penalty\ \textrm{TeV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>s</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>TeV</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{s}=13\penalty\ \textrm{TeV}</annotation></semantics></math> using the full <math id="S7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="140\penalty\ \textrm{fb}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>140</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>fb</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">140\penalty\ \textrm{fb}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> Run 2 dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite> by <math id="S7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8\penalty\ (0.4)\penalty\ \textrm{TeV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.8</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>TeV</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8\penalty\ (0.4)\penalty\ \textrm{TeV}</annotation></semantics></math> in the electron (muon) channel for QBHs in the ADD model with <math id="S7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=6</annotation></semantics></math> extra dimensions.
These limits represent the world-best sensitivity for the signals considered.</p>
</div>
</section>
